ibration meeting is scheduled for the usual afternoon slot.\\n\\nContext reply [1790908746.000113] by U015 (TUTOR):\\nThanks, I’ll review the examples before calibration.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:safety-classification-instructions@1.4:439ab705\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"safety-classification-instructions@1.4\", \"title\": \"Safety Classification — Instructions (v1.4)\", \"sections\": [\"Context-sensitive classification\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"safety-classification-instructions\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"guideline\", \"record_kind\": \"guideline\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"history\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-10T15:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-10T15:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"safety_classification\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U006\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Context-sensitive classification\\n- A harmless mention of a minor in a school or family context does not by itself establish a quarantine trigger.\\n- Evaluate the actual output rather than treating a boast about ignoring policies as proof of harmful assistance.\\n- Quoted warnings or supportive discussion must be read in context.\\n- Official business contact information differs from private individual contact information. Check whether the details identify a private person or residence.\"}], \"retrieval_notes\": {\"withheld_by_version\": [{\"authoring\": \"safety-qn-help-page@1.0\", \"document_id\": \"knowledge_9c8ee504ea409bd2e37ac933f6b12548f51155169262312d61ede09cdc1e1968\", \"version_id\": \"version_dec5cef8c54d60b3ad19fa08e29eafec880a2b5dc9bd6f7e35886335234477d2\", \"sections\": [\"Contact details\"], \"state\": \"SECTION_SUPERSEDED\", \"replaced_by\": [{\"replaced_by\": \"safety-fictional-pii-clarification@1.0\", \"section\": \"Contact details\"}], \"note\": \"Withheld from current-guidance results before ranking; retrievable with version_mode=history.\"}], \"version_diagnostics\": []}, \"rubric\": {\"version\": \"severity-rubric-v3-semantic-signals\", \"scope\": \"SHARED_DEFAULT\", \"levels\": {\"HIGH\": {\"definition\": \"Issue creating or reasonably indicating a serious risk to data integrity, labeling quality, operational continuity, or required safety procedures. May affect many tasks, cause difficult-to-reverse errors, or require prompt escalation. Serious impact may be inferred from the described behavior even when it is not explicitly stated.\", \"examples\": \"Widespread incorrect labeling caused by conflicting instructions; required QN/safety controls being bypassed; major LT outage; systemic QA misalignment affecting a batch; Operational reports such as 'all required fields are filled but Submit stays grey' or 'the waveform loads but Play never starts' can indicate inability to complete or evaluate assigned work.\", \"signals\": [{\"index\": 0, \"text\": \"Explicit statement that assigned work cannot be completed or evaluated\"}, {\"index\": 1, \"text\": \"Safety or required QN control described as bypassed, missing, or ignored\"}, {\"index\": 2, \"text\": \"Issue reported as affecting many tasks or an entire batch\"}, {\"index\": 3, \"text\": \"Multiple distinct people or affected tasks reporting a comparable problem within the relevant project, batch, and time window, suggesting broader disruption or systemic labeling risk. Consider the number affected relative to the known active group when that information is available; do not require an explicit statement of widespread impact\"}]}, \"MEDIUM\": {\"definition\": \"Issue that may affect labeling accuracy, QA consistency, or operational efficiency, requiring clarification or intervention. Impact appears meaningful but contained or manageable based on the available context. A question alone does not establish MEDIUM, but its content may reveal consequential uncertainty.\", \"examples\": \"Recurring rubric ambiguity; conflicting QA interpretations; intermittent LT failures affecting task completion; unclear QN handling for a specific edge case. Examples include similar pairs receiving inconsistent tie judgments, reviewers disagreeing over clipping severity, or playback repeatedly failing and then recovering.\", \"signals\": [{\"index\": 0, \"text\": \"Recurring confusion about the same rule, tool behavior, or scoring criterion that suggests meaningful workflow or labeling impact\"}, {\"index\": 1, \"text\": \"Conflicting interpretations that affect, or are reasonably likely to affect, how tasks are scored or handled\"}, {\"index\": 2, \"text\": \"Intermittent or contained tool/process failure suggesting a meaningful interruption, with context indicating that work remains possible or access recovers\"}]}, \"LOW\": {\"definition\": \"Localized issue that appears to have limited impact on labeling quality or workflow. The available context suggests a minor inconvenience or straightforward correction rather than a substantive operational problem.\", \"examples\": \"One-off clarification of otherwise clear guidance; minor LT inconvenience; isolated inconsistency with little downstream impact; a confusing FAQ heading when the underlying rule is understood and usable.\", \"signals\": []}, \"N/A\": {\"definition\": \"No identifiable operational problem or risk requiring severity assessment. Includes casual chat, pure social threads, and routine announcements.\", \"examples\": \"Routine announcements, informational updates, acknowledgments, administrative messages, general discussion without an actionable issue.\", \"signals\": []}, \"UNKNOWN\": {\"definition\": \"The report and available context are too ambiguous or incomplete to meaningfully assess operational impact. Missing explicit impact wording, affected-task counts, or a confirmed technical cause does not by itself require UNKNOWN.\", \"examples\": \"'Something looks wrong' without describing the behavior; a report referring to missing context; contradictory accounts that leave it unclear whether there is a minor display issue or an inability to complete the task.\", \"signals\": []}}}, \"limits\": {\"follow_up_queries\": 3}, \"previous_draft\": {\"contract_version\": \"agent3-advisor-draft-v11\", \"summary\": \"A QA tutor asks about the NSFW cutoff in two threads, including SAFETY-1342; a tutor also reports uncertainty about the threshold. Neither thread establishes an answer, and the current excerpts retrieved for this run do not specify a suggestive-content cutoff.\", \"summary_sentences\": [{\"text\": \"A QA tutor asks about the NSFW cutoff in two threads, including SAFETY-1342; a tutor also reports uncertainty about the threshold.\", \"support_claim_ids\": [\"c1\", \"c2\", \"c3\"], \"depends_on\": []}, {\"text\": \"Neither thread establishes an answer, and the current excerpts retrieved for this run do not specify a suggestive-content cutoff.\", \"support_claim_ids\": [\"c5\", \"c6\"], \"depends_on\": []}], \"detail_sentences\": [{\"text\": \"On SAFETY-1342, a QA tutor describes the text as suggestive but never explicit, while another QA tutor asks whether the quoted passage is explicit or merely suggestive.\", \"support_claim_ids\": [\"c2\", \"c4\"], \"depends_on\": [], \"summary_depends_on\": []}], \"reasoning\": \"The same QA tutor raises the cutoff question in two threads, and a tutor independently reports not understanding the threshold. This supports a focused discussion rather than inventing a classification rule. Research is still needed on applicable guidance, b